config BR2_PACKAGE_BATOCERA_HOME
	bool "batocera-home"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON3
	select BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON_EVDEV
	select BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON_PSUTIL
	select BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON_PYGAME2
	select BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON_DBUS_FAST		# controls limusic over MPRIS from Home's Music view
	select BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON_AIOHTTP		# downloads limusic's own album art
	help
	  Home: holds the gamepad Guide button (or the keyboard Home key) as a pause/resume
	  hotkey for every emulator, independent of whatever quit hotkey that emulator's own
	  config happens to have. Freezes the whole running process tree (SIGSTOP/SIGCONT) and
	  shows a Resume/Quit screen while it's frozen, with a Music view to control the
	  background Limusic player (see the "limusic" package/service).

	  EmulationStation's own Start/Space menu (see batocera-emulationstation's
	  GuiMenu title patch) is branded "HOME" too, so both entry points read as one
	  consistent system - EmulationStation still does all the actual menu work
	  (settings, scraper, network, etc.) unchanged, this package doesn't touch any
	  of that.
